  quantumProcessingE2e_s17: "Every combination is decided by five codes at once — involution (a host answered 304 to the hash the request named: the content proven equal at the edge, nothing computed or sent), any (the fastest answer, unchecked), first-two-agree (the race ends when two copies agree), tree-reference (the tree's answer once the fastest host confirms it), majority (every copy) — and the fastest code whose decision is the consensus wins; a tie goes to the stronger code. An uncorrectable combination lists its possibilities: every value some copies hold.",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s18: "The rules, judged on every run: ⟦0⟧. ⟦1⟧",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s19: "All ⟦0⟧ combinations followed every rule.",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s20: "| Combination | Tool | Outcome | Winner | Possibilities |",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s21: " — a migration in flight: hosts on different versions are copies of one value, and uptime is whole while every combination still agrees",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s22: "| Host | Version | Copies | Involutions (304) | Flips | Erasures | Refusals | Median ms |",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s23: "| Toolbox | Agree | Corrected | Erased | Uncorrectable |",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s24: "Each error is a UUID over its kind, host, combination and hashes; the stream `e2e.ndjson` carries these lines and no bodies.",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s25: "| UUID | Kind | Host | Tool | Expected | Got | Syndrome |",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s8: "the host did not answer: not deployed, or the network; an erasure is decoded from the other copies",
  quantumProcessingE2e_s9: "the host answers differently from the majority: deploy the tree there, or the result depends on the host (tenant, time)",
  quantumProcessingE2e_says1: "⟦0⟧ used ⟦1⟧ copies at ⟦2⟧ ms, but the ⟦3⟧th arrived at ⟦4⟧ ms",
  quantumProcessingE2e_says2: "a winner was named without a consensus",
  quantumProcessingE2e_statement5: "⟦0⟧ ⟦1⟧: no majority among the tree and ⟦2⟧ host(s) (⟦3⟧; tree=⟦4⟧)",
  quantumProcessingE2e_statement7: "⟦0⟧: ⟦1⟧ flip(s), ⟦2⟧ erasure(s), ⟦3⟧ refusal(s) over ⟦4⟧ copies; the syndrome names it",
  quantumProcessingE2e_value4: "HTTP 304 unverified: the hash or the address the host echoed is not the one held here",
