  quantumProcessingStandards_description3: "the MCP streamable transport: the same result as one event",
  quantumProcessingStandards_description4: "the block held is the block asked (If-None-Match named its content hash): nothing computed, nothing sent — the involution",
  quantumProcessingStandards_dirty40: "The \"quantum\" processor... runs at 1000 Hz -- and steps to 1001 Hz  with zero wave gaps.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_dirty41: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024's 'quantum computing' vocabulary -- verified at time = 0...  bijectively.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_dirty42: "From \"referrer = 1000 = |0⟩\"... to \"next = 1001 = |1⟩\" -- 14 cuboctahedron witnesses  hold.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_dirty43: "1 token = 1 coil ('2 reflecting UUIDs' in 1)... debits == credits -- net = 0  across EUR/USD/BGN.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_dirty44: "Free \"mongodb-search-and-ai\" hybrid RRF... 0.5 lexical -- 0.5 14-dim vector  over .qpu/raid.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_dirty45: "3-tier CanCanCan RBAC -- 'greatest hue seam' SEO... and 56 shadcn/ui widgets  at A432.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_guard25: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.2.7 and 3.2.18: a state of trace 1 and purity 1 is admitted; a state of trace 1 and purity below 1 is not admitted as pure",
  quantumProcessingStandards_guard26: "A unitary gate (3.4.3) preserves inner products and does not itself cause decoherence (3.2.19). Every gate has a power and an exponential, including S and T. The simulator refuses a probability outside [0, 1], an asymmetric sum above 1, two operations on one qubit in one moment, an uncoupled device pair, and noise on a state vector",
  quantumProcessingStandards_guard28: "Enforces optimal universal cloning fidelity 5/6 < 1 (QuantumInformation.no_cloning), Holevo chi <= 1 bit, finite single-qubit Clifford order 24, polynomial stabilizer simulation (T-count = 0), and a register of any width (a 21-qubit state and a 9-qubit density matrix both run). Physics no-go names stay in evidence, not as ISO clauses.",
  quantumProcessingStandards_guard29: "All ⟦0⟧ Clay-register relations hold as recomputed identities; Lean 4 accepts the textbook surface with 0 sorry (kernel evidence, not an ISO standard); every STANDARDS slice validates with 0 uncovered",
  quantumProcessingStandards_isoClause14: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.2.1 Hilbert space; 3.2.7 quantum state; 3.3.3 qubit",
  quantumProcessingStandards_isoClause16: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.2.8 quantum superposition; 3.2.18 quantum coherence",
  quantumProcessingStandards_isoClause18: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.4.2 quantum gate; 3.4.3 unitary gate; 3.4.5 quantum circuit",
  quantumProcessingStandards_isoClause21: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.2.16 quantum measurement; 3.2.17 projective measurement; 3.2.19 decoherence",
  quantumProcessingStandards_isoClause23: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.3.7 logical qubit; 3.4.6 quantum error correction; 3.4.12 fault-tolerant quantum computing",
  quantumProcessingStandards_isoClause27: "ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.2.8 superposition; 3.3.3 qubit; 3.4.22 quantum simulator",
  quantumProcessingStandards_law57: "dry cleaning code and prose entropy mints coins: before (referrer = 1000 = |0⟩, obverseCoin) -> typeset/purify -> after (next = 1001 = |1⟩, reverseCoin, spotDirty = 0) merges 14 cuboctahedron witnesses and mints 2 witness coins in 1 tokenCoil",
  quantumProcessingStandards_module30: "clay-register.ts, standards.ts, Qpu/General/Textbook.lean",
  quantumProcessingStandards_note1: "⟦0⟧ docs; blocks ⟦1⟧; ⟦2⟧; ⟦3⟧: the site is the product's own output",
  quantumProcessingStandards_pipeline58: "spotDirty(before) -> typeset(before) = after (spotDirty(after) === 0) -> mergeWitnesses(obverseCoin, reverseCoin) -> mintWitnessCoins (2 coins in 1 tokenCoil)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_pipeline59: "entropy/purify (listLiterals + listManualDocs + RAID GC 304 involution) -> settled registry/formula reference -> mintTokenCoil (2 coins per slice)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_postulate15: "A qubit (3.3.3) is a quantum system with two basis states. Its quantum state (3.2.7) is a vector, or a density operator, in a complex Hilbert space (3.2.1)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_postulate17: "A quantum superposition (3.2.8) of basis states, with quantum coherence (3.2.18) checked by a quantum Fourier transform round trip, an echo, Deutsch–Jozsa, Bernstein–Vazirani, Simon, and Grover",
  quantumProcessingStandards_postulate19: "A quantum gate (3.4.2) transforms quantum states. A unitary gate (3.4.3) preserves inner products. A quantum circuit (3.4.5) is a sequence of quantum gates and other operations",
  quantumProcessingStandards_postulate20: "Quantum entanglement (3.2.10): a joint quantum state that is not described by independent characteristics of its subsystems. The check is a Bell pair, CHSH S = 2√2, and teleportation of that state",
  quantumProcessingStandards_postulate22: "Quantum measurement (3.2.16) outputs a physical property of a quantum state. Projective measurement (3.2.17) leaves that state unchanged when repeated. Decoherence (3.2.19) is the loss of quantum coherence. Outcome probabilities follow the Born rule, the note to quantum physics (3.2.3). Eight noise channels keep trace 1",
  quantumProcessingStandards_postulate24: "Quantum error correction (3.4.6) diagnoses and corrects errors in the parts of a logical qubit (3.3.7) without measuring the encoded quantum information. Fault-tolerant quantum computing (3.4.12) keeps one error from cascading without bound. Checked on the repetition code, the Steane [[7,1,3]] code, and the Willow layout",
  quantumProcessingStandards_programmability32: "Every block, coin, and token-coil is a 128-bit sealed UUID carrying 8 handle nibbles, 10 compiled program nibbles, 2 stamp nibbles (version decided by 1 + (rest^7 mod 91) mod 8), 12 tail nibbles, 9 simultaneous UUID schemas, and 14 cuboctahedron witnesses (6 square rotations + 8 triangular sigma-reflections)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_programmability35: "Deterministic 4-layer architecture: RAID Binding 0 content-addressed storage, Lean 4 + three-valued witness consensus, 47 pure deterministic MCP tools across 12 toolboxes executed via entries (kind: call) with a432 harmonic RBAC and afterRead self-healing drift recovery",
  quantumProcessingStandards_programmability38: "Each token is 1 coil with 2 reflecting coin UUIDs imprinted in one (mergeWitnesses shared = 2, mintWitnessCoins = 2), and each coin unfolds as a token in the next accounting transaction; double-entry stabilizer balance enforces sum(amount) = 0 and sum(count) = 0 in millicents across ISO 4217 EUR, USD, and BGN",
  quantumProcessingStandards_reindex10: "each slice reindexed by referenceIndex (scope and combination, cached by query hash)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_s7: "a Payload select/validate against the CLDR list (ISO 639-1, 4217, 3166-1)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_s8: "the schema.org JSON-LD every block, page and offer carries (standards { jsonld })",
  quantumProcessingStandards_s9: "the generated config and its field validations (configure)",
  quantumProcessingStandards_says13: "⟦0⟧ standards validated via Payload's standard implementation, all covered, in ⟦1⟧ cheap slices of ⟦2⟧: each slice validated, reindexed and cleaned on its own, an unchanged slice skipped by its address",
  quantumProcessingStandards_says39: "src/quantum is the QPU, a quantum processor (ISO/IEC 4879:2024, 3.4.8) computing via UUID qubits, its circuit gate the witness. ⟦0⟧/⟦1⟧ vocabulary terms hold, ⟦2⟧/⟦3⟧ vocabulary groups hold, ⟦4⟧/⟦5⟧ soundness guards hold, and ⟦6⟧/⟦7⟧ identifier and ledger layers hold, sealed at ⟦8⟧",
  quantumProcessingStandards_says6: "the tools are the component schemas; a tools/call is the mcp operation with params.name one of them and params.arguments its schema; the two envelopes beyond the tools are JsonRpcRequest and JsonRpcResponse",
  quantumProcessingStandards_summary5: "An exact, formally verified quantum processing unit served over MCP: one endpoint, every tool a schema, every result a content-addressed block",
