  quantumProcessingToolboxesRepository_shows125: "Fixture facts against fixture answers: two local branches unpushed, one remote branch not here, a local tag not pushed, a remote tag not fetched, a moved tag, a release whose tag is gone, a version with a tag and no release, a Zenodo version without a release, a second workspace, the registry behind the tree, a red workflow at the remote, two workflows only at the remote: fourteen leads.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesRepository_source2: "OpenAlex, sealed per theorem in the docket (textbook { claims })",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_description1: "schema.org JSON-LD, pure: for a block (tool, id, description), a page (url, title, description, uuid?) or an offer of the catalogue (product, variant, currency). The author a Person with an ORCID, the licence a URL, dates ISO 8601, languages ISO 639-1, currencies ISO 4217. Every tools/call result already carries its block's JSON-LD in _meta.jsonLd; every documentation page carries its own in its head.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_description10: "the paths to classify (an array, or one per line), the files read by the client as files: each path → the ISO dimensions it cites, the unclassified named",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_description2: "The tree's ISO codes validated against the CLDR lists a client fetched (languages ISO 639, currencies ISO 4217, territories ISO 3166-1): every locale of the language toolbox, every currency of the catalogue, the tenants' countries. Without the lists: what would be checked and where the lists are. A code the standard does not know is a lead, never a guess.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_description8: "Validate against all standards via Payload's standard implementation, in the cheapest possible slices: every standard (the vocabularies, the ISO code lists, the references) with the Payload mechanism that validates it, split into content-addressed slices so validation, reindexing and cleanup run per slice (a page, a job) — the cheapest unit, an unchanged slice skipped by its address (the 304 involution), never the whole at once. online: true asks the ISO Open Data page. A page answer yields the JSONLines link that page publishes. A file answer verifies each ISO dimension by a reference in that file and defines it by the English title and the scope. The catalogue number is the row id.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_description9: "true: the ISO Open Data page. { status, text }: that page, or the JSONLines file the page linked",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_idea11: "the standards fused: schema.org on every block, page and offer; ISO 8601, 639-1, 4217 and 3166-1 in every date, language, price and country, validated against the CLDR lists discovery reads as contracts",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_instructions16: "jsonld needs no fetch. codes: the client fetches the three CLDR documents the plan names (GET, free, no credential) and calls codes with them; a code the standard does not know is a lead. The discover step reads schema.org's vocabulary and the CLDR lists as contracts; every tools/call result carries _meta.jsonLd and every documentation page a JSON-LD script.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_reason4: "rename the locale to its code, or it is a dialect to tag under its language",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_reason6: "the catalogue prices in codes the standard names",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s17: "server only: JSON-LD shapes on fixtures; CLDR fixtures read into code sets; the tree's codes validated",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s18: "client → server: the CLDR lists come from Unicode's repository",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s19: "toolbox → toolbox: offers come from the billing catalogue, locales from the language toolbox, the contracts from discovery",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s20: "CreativeWork with ORCID author, ISO 8601 date, ISO 639-1 language",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s21: "WebPage with identifier and locale",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s22: "Offer in ISO 4217 with a yearly UnitPriceSpecification",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s23: "locales ⟦0⟧ valid, currencies ⟦1⟧ valid, territory XX unknown",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s24: "without the lists nothing is called unknown",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s25: "the vocabulary and a CLDR list are told apart",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_s26: "⟦0⟧ dimensions asked through the ISO Open Data page; a published row verifies, a title and a scope define it, and a base document is kept ahead of an amendment",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_says7: "⟦0⟧ of ⟦1⟧ file(s) cite an ISO dimension; ⟦2⟧ unclassified, named",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_shows12: "validateStandards validates against all standards via Payload's standard implementation, in the cheapest possible slices: every standard (a codes list by a select/validate against CLDR, a vocabulary by schema.org JSON-LD, a reference by the generated config and its field validations) covered, split into content-addressed slices of six so validation, reindexing (referenceIndex) and cleanup (purify, the RAID GC) run per slice as a job — the cheapest unit, an unchanged slice skipped by its address; the covered and the uncovered make the standards.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_shows13: "Every ISO dimension is asked of the ISO Open Data page. The deliverables file is the JSONLines link that page publishes. No catalogue number is kept here. Nothing is verified until that file is the answer. Research and citations are asked of the DOI ecosystem: ISO 690 names the elements, ISO 26324 names the identifier.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_shows14: "The ISO Open Data page is the way in. The next request is the JSONLines address that page published, and the dimensions stay unverified until that file is the answer.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_shows15: "One row of the open dataset verifies the dimension its reference names. The catalogue page is that row's id. The dimensions the file does not name stay unverified.",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_statement3: "locale ⟦0⟧ is not an ISO 639 code CLDR names",
  quantumProcessingToolboxesStandards_statement5: "currency ⟦0⟧ is not an ISO 4217 code CLDR names",
  quantumProcessingUnitConstants_says1: "no table header: the page changed or was not read",
  quantumProcessingUnitConstants_says2: "⟦0⟧ constants of the ⟦1⟧ CODATA adjustment as integers, each sealed: ⟦2⟧ exact by definition, ⟦3⟧ measured with their stated uncertainty kept; a seal proves a value is the one published, never that it is truer",
  quantumProcessingUnitIndex_unscoped1: "⟦0⟧ is the main unscoped account: every tenant, super-admin; never a tenant",
